<section class="section theme-white">
  <div class="container hc-narrow">
    <h2>We look at how production finance actually works in your organisation</h2>
    <p class="hc-lead">Every production company works differently. We start by understanding how budgets, costs, forecasts, approvals and reporting currently move through your organisation.</p>
    <ul class="hc-topics">
      <li>Budgeting</li>
      <li>Actual spend</li>
      <li>Budget versus actuals</li>
      <li>Forecasting</li>
      <li>Approvals</li>
      <li>Reporting</li>
      <li>Multiple productions</li>
      <li>Financial visibility</li>
      <li>Manual work and reconciliation</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="hc-aside-note">One question we always ask: how do you know today where a running production will end up financially? The answer usually says more about a process than any list of tools.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section theme-light">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-heading">You leave with a clearer picture of what can be improved</h2>
    <p class="section-intro hc-lead">During the session we note what we see. Afterwards you get a short written summary: the three main opportunities, where unnecessary manual work or financial risk sits, and which improvement is likely to have the most effect first.</p>
    <div class="cards-grid cards-3">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Reduce manual work</h3>
        <p>Identify processes involving unnecessary spreadsheets, duplication or reconciliation.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Improve financial visibility</h3>
        <p>See where budget, actual and forecast information could be easier to access and understand.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Improve control</h3>
        <p>Identify opportunities to improve approvals, budget versions and financial processes.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section theme-white">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-heading">How it works</h2>
    <ol class="hc-steps">
      <li>
        <span class="hc-steps-num">1</span>
        <h3>A few short questions</h3>
        <p>Around two minutes: who you are, what you produce and where the work sits today. Then you pick a time that suits you.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="hc-steps-num">2</span>
        <h3>45 minutes together, on a call</h3>
        <p>We talk through how production finance currently works within your organisation and identify areas of friction, manual work or risk. A conversation, not a questionnaire: most of what matters comes up while you describe how a production actually runs.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="hc-steps-num">3</span>
        <h3>Receive your findings</h3>
        <p>We summarise the main opportunities and practical improvements we identified. If Tubes could help with any of these areas, we can show you how. There is no obligation to continue.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section theme-teal">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-heading">Areas we assess</h2>
    <p class="section-intro hc-lead">Six areas, worked through in order. The point is not to grade you, but to see where financial control is currently held together by hand.</p>
    <div class="hc-areas">
      <article class="hc-area">
        <span class="hc-area-num">01</span>
        <h3>Budget structure and version control</h3>
        <p>How budgets are built, how changes are made, and how you know which version is the current one.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="hc-area">
        <span class="hc-area-num">02</span>
        <h3>Budget to production handover</h3>
        <p>What happens after a budget is approved, and how the people spending the money get a working budget they can use.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="hc-area">
        <span class="hc-area-num">03</span>
        <h3>Actuals and reconciliation</h3>
        <p>How real costs come in, how they are coded, and how much manual work it takes to match them back to the budget.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="hc-area">
        <span class="hc-area-num">04</span>
        <h3>Forecasting</h3>
        <p>How commitments, costs to date and remaining costs add up to an expected final cost, and how often that picture is refreshed.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="hc-area">
        <span class="hc-area-num">05</span>
        <h3>Approvals and controls</h3>
        <p>Who may commit spend, who may change a budget, and how that is recorded.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="hc-area">
        <span class="hc-area-num">06</span>
        <h3>Reporting and visibility</h3>
        <p>Who gets reliable financial information, in what form, and how long it takes to produce.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="hc-areas-legend">We label each area <span class="chip chip-mint">Strong</span> <span class="chip chip-amber">Could improve</span> <span class="chip chip-lavender">Opportunity</span> based on what you tell us. We never publish company names or findings.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section theme-white">
  <div class="container hc-narrow">
    <h2>And if we see somewhere Tubes could help, we will show you</h2>
    <p>Tubes is production finance software designed to bring budgets, actuals, forecasting, approvals and reporting together.</p>
    <p>During the Health Check we do not give a standard software demonstration. We first understand your process. If Tubes can solve one of the problems we identify, we can show you the relevant part of the platform.</p>
    <p class="hc-tubes-link"><a href="/platform/">Read about the platform</a> if you would rather look first.</p>
  </div>
</section>

